-- title:
--   Shrinking an affine chart: minimal primes contracting into 𝔪
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a noetherian commutative ring, $F$ a field with an $R$-algebra structure, and $B$ an $R$-subalgebra of $F$ which is finitely generated as an $R$-algebra. Let $I$ be an ideal of $R$ and let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a prime ideal of $B$ containing the image ideal $I\cdot B$, i.e. the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $I$ under $R \to B$. The assertion is that there exists an element $h$ of $F$ lying in $B$, whose corresponding element of $B$ does not belong to $\mathfrak{m}$, with the following property: writing $B' = R[B \cup \{h^{-1}\}]$ for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $B$ together with the inverse $h^{-1}$ of $h$ in $F$, every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $B'$ that is a minimal prime over the ideal $I\cdot B'$ generated by the image of $I$ in $B'$ satisfies $\mathfrak{q} \cap B \subseteq \mathfrak{m}$; formally, for every $b \in B$, if the element $b$, viewed in $B'$ via the inclusion $B \subseteq B'$, lies in $\mathfrak{q}$, then $b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}$.
--
--   This is a prime-avoidance statement of the usual geometric shape: an affine chart $\operatorname{Spec} B$ may be shrunk to the principal open $h \neq 0$ through the point $\mathfrak{m}$ so that every irreducible component of the closed subscheme cut out by $I$ passes through that point. It is used in the construction of node charts for the semistable model of the full-level modular curve, where it is invoked by the local statements comparing stalks at points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subalgebra_exists_notMem_forall_minimalPrimes_map_le_of_fg.lean

